@@ -38,10 +38,21 @@
 
 Highlighting is controlled with text widget tags, that are called highlight classes.
 The [arg class] is a tag name and can be configured like any text widget tag.
 Four types of highlight classes are supported. All highlight classes are automatically used
 by the [method highlight] method of the widget.
+[para]
+Text is highlighted when it is inserted (unless option [option -highlight] is false
+or [method fastinsert] is used).
+Adding, changing or deleting a highlight class does not rehighlight text which is
+already in the widget; call [arg pathName] [method highlight] [const {1.0 end}]
+after filling the widget or after changing the highlight classes.
+[para]
+A class created with [cmd ::ctext::addHighlightClassForRegexp] holds a single pattern;
+adding it again with the same class name replaces the previous pattern. To highlight
+several patterns, use different class names or combine the patterns into one
+with regular expression alternation.
 
 [list_begin definitions]
 
 [call [cmd ::ctext::addHighlightClass] [arg pathName] [arg class] [arg color] [arg keywordlist]]
 
@@ -73,10 +84,16 @@
 [call [cmd ::ctext::addHighlightClassForRegexp] [arg pathName] [arg class] [arg color] [arg pattern]]
 
 Add a highlighting class [arg class] to the ctext widget [arg pathName].
 The highlighting will be done with the color [arg color]. All text parts matching the regexp [arg pattern]
 will be highlighted.
+Embedded options can be used, e.g. a pattern starting with [const (?i)] matches case-insensitively.
+
+[example {
+	# highlight Fortran keywords in any case
+	::ctext::addHighlightClassForRegexp .t keywords blue {(?i)\m(subroutine|function|end)\M}
+ }]
 
 [call [cmd ::ctext::clearHighlightClasses] [arg pathName]]
 
 Remove all highlight classes from the widget [arg pathName].
 

